 revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 145% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.4526468293731496},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4468487.66},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Sabra Healthcare REIT (SBRA) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/what-sabra-healthcare-reit-sbra-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794003299.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.802,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Did Raised 2026 Guidance Just Shift Sabra Health Care REIT's (SBRA) Investment Narrative?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nasdaq-sbra/sabra-health-care-reit/news/did-raised-2026-guidance-just-shift-sabra-health-care-reits","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793950647.725,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.941,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Sabra Healthcare REIT (NASDAQ:SBRA) Issues FY 2026 Earnings Guidance","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/sabra-healthcare-reit-nasdaqsbra-issues-fy-2026-earnings-guidance.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793883417.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","legal"]},{"title":"Sabra Health Care REIT (SBRA) Stock Looks Overvalued As Its 107% Five Year Run Continues","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/sabra-health-care-reit-sbra-161656467.html","date":"2026-11-04"